# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...except the template. `.env*` above swallowed it, which meant the one
# file that documents the two vars a deployer needs (NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL,
# RESEND_API_KEY) never shipped. It holds PLACEHOLDERS ONLY - verified
# against .env.local before this line was written. Keep it that way.
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# CAD source — 75 MB, and git never forgets
#
# `source-assets/Residential_complex/art66.dwg` (14 MB) and the `art66.dxf`
# (61 MB) the operator converted from it are the INPUT to
# `scripts/extract-floor-plan.py`, not part of the site. Committing them would
# put 75 MB into history permanently — every clone, every CI run, forever, and
# unremovable without rewriting history.
#
# What the site actually needs is `src/content/floor-plan.generated.ts`, which
# is 60 KB and IS committed. Keep the CAD files on disk; re-run the extractor
# when they change. If a rebuild is ever needed from scratch, the operator has
# the originals — see the header of the extractor for what it reads.
*.dwg
*.dxf

# =============================================================================
# CLIENT SOURCE MATERIAL - THE WHOLE FOLDER, NOT JUST THE CAD
# =============================================================================
# `*.dwg` / `*.dxf` above stopped the two biggest files and nothing else. The
# rest of `source-assets/` is 43 MB of site videos, six CAMERA renders, and
# `art66.jpg`. `mo-haj/ankaa` is a PUBLIC repository; none of this is the site,
# all of it is the association's own raw material, and git never forgets.
#
# |X| art66.jpg IS AN AI IMAGE AND IS NOT THIS BUILDING. It was measured at
# roughly a 20% match - the interior walls do not align with the architect's
# plan. Publishing it anywhere, including as a file sitting in a folder named
# `Residential_complex`, invites exactly the mistake of reading it as a
# photograph of the real thing. It stays on disk and out of git.
#
# What the site actually needs from this folder is already committed:
# `src/content/floor-plan.generated.ts` (60 KB) and the images under `public/`.
/source-assets/

# Generated by the plan pipeline - regenerate, never commit.
#   scripts/floor-plan.json   <- JSON_OUT of extract-floor-plan.py
#   exports/                  <- npm run plan:png
/scripts/floor-plan.json
/exports/

# Python bytecode from scripts/extract-floor-plan.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
